@startuml BC-07_Dashboard

note as ImplementationNote
  The Dashboard bounded context is implemented as a single
  static view component with no backend API integration.
  All data (stats, appointments, lab orders, stock alerts)
  is hardcoded sample data. Chart geometry is computed via
  local SVG helper functions. i18n is used for labels.
  There is no Pinia store, API, assembler, or domain model
  specific to this bounded context.
end note

package "dashboard.presentation.views" {
  class DashboardView <<view>> {
    - today: ComputedRef<string>
    - stats: object[]
    - appointments: object[]
    - labOrders: object[]
    - stockAlerts: object[]
    - recetasData: number[]
    - ventasData: number[]
    - yTicks: number[]
    - weekRevenue: number[]
    - months: ComputedRef<string[]>
    - weekDays: ComputedRef<string[]>
    - xLabels: ComputedRef<object[]>
    - bars: ComputedRef<object[]>
    - barYTicks: object[]
    - recPts: string
    - venPts: string
    - recAreaPts: string
    - venAreaPts: string
    - gridLines: object[]
    - recDots: object[]
    - venDots: object[]
    + lx(i: number): number
    + ly(v: number): number
    + polyPts(data: number[]): string
    + bx(i: number): number
    + bh(v: number): number
    + by(v: number): number
  }
}

package "dashboard.presentation" {
  class DashboardRoutes <<configuration>> {
    + path: "/panel"
    + name: "dashboard"
    + component: DashboardView
    + meta.title: "Panel de Control"
  }
}

DashboardView --> DashboardRoutes : registered in
DashboardView ..> Router : uses (useRouter)
DashboardView ..> I18n : uses (useI18n, tm)

note right of DashboardView
  Stat cards: totalPatients, patientsToday,
  monthlyRevenue, pendingLabOrders (all static).

  Line chart: recetas vs ventas (6-month SVG).
  Bar chart: weekly revenue per day (SVG).

  No real-time data — values are placeholders
  until an Analytics API is implemented.
end note

@enduml
